      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes complete sense that you don't want to call this a \"phase\" when your core identity feels shattered, like a book you've finished with nothing left to write. That specific grief of losing yourself in service of others can leave you feeling like a ghost in your own life once the confidence and purpose you built vanish. While finding a new reason to keep going immediately is impossible, it is still possible to find healing simply by acknowledging this darkness is a legitimate part of the recovery process, not a permanent sentence.",
      "source": "target",
